title: "arm-benefit-net: treatment-conditioned deep learning on public oncology clinical-trial transcriptomics"
type: software
version: "v0.1.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24246595
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24246595"
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/FelipeMSD/arm-benefit-net"
authors:
  - family-names: "Morillo Sanz Dias"
    given-names: "Felipe"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5232-4312"
abstract: >
  PyTorch framework and reproducible analysis asking whether pre-treatment tumour
  transcriptomes identify which trial arm benefits which patient. A multi-task network
  (ArmNet) is benchmarked under nested, patient-level cross-validation on 741 randomised
  HER2-negative patients from I-SPY2 (GSE194040), with randomisation-based benefit metrics,
  Integrated Gradients explanations, and external transfer, deep Cox survival modelling
  and BulkFormer embeddings in IMvigor210. Includes a Nature-style report and an
  11-lesson PyTorch course.
